  "slug": "spatial-transcriptomics-6c8f",
  "summary": "Seven preprints combine transcriptomic, proteomic and perturbation data in tumours, with resources for PDAC and PTM co-variation alongside mechanistic studies.",
  "synthesis": "The current items share a focus on integrating multiple molecular layers to define tumour regulatory states, not on live-tissue or isoform-resolved sampling. Resource-oriented work includes PDAC BioPortal, which unifies bulk, single-nucleus and spatial PDAC cohorts, and PTMlink, which scores glycosylation–phosphorylation co-variation across 1,211 tumour proteomes. A TNBC framework combines Perturb-seq CRISPRi responses with TF binding priors, nominating CTCF, MYC and AP-1 members as master regulators. Serum proteomics with intact N-glycoproteomics, analysed with a DTS strategy, links glycan remodelling to ovarian cancer. Mechanistic and association studies include KDM3B-mediated H3K9me2 removal at the ERBB3 promoter in cholangiocarcinoma, and Mendelian randomization with single-cell data linking midkine to PDAC. A breast–ovarian GEO integration prioritizes hub genes and food-derived compounds.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
